# Out-of-tree host state the n8n-claude runtime must bind into the container
# (read by provision.sh gen-override). Ariadne's pipelines keep every artifact
# they produce — detect_entrypoints output, triage state and its run results,
# the index cache — under ~/.ariadne, outside the repo. Unbound, that state
# lands in the container's writable layer and is destroyed by any recreate,
# which silently resets the workflow step markers that make a re-run a no-op.
#
# Not path parity: the container's HOME is /home/node, so the host path and the
# container path are genuinely different and both must be named.
~/.ariadne:/home/node/.ariadne
